children of Israel, twelve, according to their names, like the engravings of a signet; every one with his name shall they be according to the twelve tribes.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses—„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙZAnd thou shalt make upon the breastplate chains at the ends of wreathen work of pure gold.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ{And thou shalt make upon the breastplate two rings of gold, and shalt put the two rings on the two ends of the breastplate.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙmAnd thou shalt put the two wreathen chains of gold in the two rings which are on the ends of the breastplate.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‘And the other two ends of the two wreathen chains thou shalt fasten in the two ouches, and put them on the shoulderpieces of the ephod before it.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¤And thou shalt make two rings of gold, and thou shalt put them upon the two ends of the breastplate in the border thereof, which is in the side of the ephod inward.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÖAnd two other rings of gold thou shalt make, and shalt put them on the two sides of the ephod underneath, toward the forepart thereof, over against the other coupling thereof, above the curious girdle of the ephod.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÖAnd they shall bind the breastplate by the rings thereof unto the rings of the ephod with a lace of blue, that it may be above the curious girdle of the ephod, and that the breastplate be not loosed from the ephod.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¹And Aaron shall bear the names of the children of Israel in the breastplate of judgment upon his heart, when he goeth in unto the holy place, for a memorial before the LORD continually.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙûAnd thou shalt put in the breastplate of judgment the Urim and the Thummim; and they shall be upon Aaron's heart, when he goeth in before the LORD: and Aaron shall bear the judgment of the children of Israel upon his heart before the LORD continually.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse#¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ6And thou shalt make the robe of the ephod all of blue.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¾And there shall be an hole in the top of it, in the midst thereof: it shall have a binding of woven work round about the hole of it, as it were the hole of an habergeon, that it be not rent.¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¬And beneath upon the hem of it thou shalt make pomegranates of blue, and of purple, and of scarlet, round about the hem thereof; and bells of gold between them round about:¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙga golden bell and a pomegranate, a golden bell and a pomegranate, upon the hem of the robe round about.¦layout ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ£And it shall be upon Aaron to minister: and his sound shall be heard when he goeth in unto the holy place before the LORD, and when he cometh out, that he die not.¦layout ªlast_verse#…¤book§chapter«first_verse$ªlast_verse&¦verses“„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙsAnd thou shalt make a plate of pure gold, and grave upon it, like the engravings of a signet, HOLINESS TO THE Lord.¦layout ªlast_verse$„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙqAnd thou shalt put it on a blue lace, that it may be upon the mitre; upon the forefront of the mitre it shall be.¦layout ªlast_verse%„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙóAnd it shall be upon Aaron's forehead, that Aaron may bear the iniquity of the holy things, which the children of Israel shall hallow in all their holy gifts; and it shall be always upon his forehead, that they may be accepted before the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse&…¤book§chapter«first_verse'ªlast_verse'¦verses‘„¥verse'¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‹And thou shalt embroider the coat of fine linen, and thou shalt make the mitre of fine linen, and thou shalt make the girdle of needlework.¦layout ªlast_verse'…¤book§chapter«first_verse(ªlast_verse+¦verses”„¥verse(¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‘And for Aaron's sons thou shalt make coats, and thou shalt make for them girdles, and bonnets shalt thou make for them, for glory and for beauty.¦layout ªlast_verse(„¥verse)¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¼And thou shalt put them upon Aaron thy brother, and his sons with him; and shalt anoint them, and consecrate them, and sanctify them, that they may minister unto me in the priest's office.¦layout ªlast_verse)„¥verse*¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙwAnd thou shalt make them linen breeches to cover their nakedness; from the loins even unto the thighs they shall reach:¦layout ªlast_verse*„¥verse+¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚand they shall be upon Aaron, and upon his sons, when they come in unto the tabernacle of the congregation, or when they come near unto the altar to minister in the holy place; that they bear not iniquity, and die: it shall be a statute for ever unto him and his seed after him.¦layout ªlast_verse+